    "customfield_12311020": null,
    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12363401/comment/12475096",
          "id": "12475096",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "\nThe no-argument constructors for Native/SimpleFSLockFactory were\nremoved as part of LUCENE-771 (store write.lock in index directory by\ndefault).  These APIs were never released (ie only available in the\ntrunk builds).\n\nSince there is no longer a notion of the \"global default lock\ndirectory\", I'm not really sure how to (or whether to) fix this: these\nlock factories really need to know the directory to store their lock\nfiles in.\n\nThe fallback is to instantiate the LockFactory ahead of time and pass\nit into FSDirectory.getDirectory().  Is that fallback workable here?\n\nI'd lean towards \"won't fix\" on this unless someone can suggest a good\nsolution.  That property can still be used for other lock factory\ninstances that require no arguments on construction.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-02-22T17:30:13.353+0000",
          "updated": "2007-02-22T17:30:13.353+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12363401/comment/12475130",
          "id": "12475130",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "I'm not sure if i understand what the bug is ... as far as i can tell, LockFactory didnt' exist in 2.0.\n\n(Since we've been actively moving away from specifying class instances with System Properties, i'm suprised to even see code in 2.1 that allows the LockFactory to be specified in that way.)\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "created": "2007-02-22T19:26:15.078+0000",
          "updated": "2007-02-22T19:26:15.078+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12363401/comment/12475138",
          "id": "12475138",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Actually it was your response to the original proposal for the LockFactory changes that caused me to leave the system property path in there :)\n\n    http://www.gossamer-threads.com/lists/lucene/java-dev/37401#37401\n\nI think having both options can be helpful, but, system properties are dangerous because they are global so perhaps going forward we should try not add any new system properties...",
